@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@ Integration/M5/J714s-Normal-System/prepare /absolute/new/build-directory
 
 The command fetches immutable omacom/omarchy-pkgs commit `30a33ee435db8f4a158ca41f82e91cc34bcd2e3b` into a local Git cache, verifies the resolved commit, extracts the selected recipes, applies the checksummed `recipes.patch` and `runtime-pair.patch`, then copies the frozen kernel, loader and Mesa inputs. Its only network access is that pinned Git fetch. It does not build, install, enroll, contact a Mac or publish. Existing destinations are refused. Build the copies with ordinary Arch `makepkg` in an appropriate aarch64 build environment. Their package names/providers/conflicts stay normal, so do not install these private candidates on an ordinary supported Mac.
 
+After the 15 package archives and reviewed Recovery/Engine inputs exist, [`tools/finish-inputs.py`](tools/finish-inputs.py) validates them against the checked-in package manifest and source provenance, verifies the approved developer signer, signs the candidate-set metadata, and writes the developer-only `.tar.zst` build-input bundle. It checks that the builder SHA is the current published `origin/main`. The signing home is read only for signing; the bundle contains the signed package set, public trust material, Recovery app, Engine archive and provenance, never the private key. Use `--help` for the required local input paths. The helper does not build packages or an image, publish a supported release, change the catalog or qualify hardware.
+
 ## Exact sources
 
 | Component | Public baseline and private source closure | Normal integration |
